lient.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503, making at most 3 attempts in total. I tested it against a local HTTP server and every case behaved as intended.\n\nHow it works:\n- **Retry trigger:** only a 503. Any other HTTP error, such as 500 or 404, is raised straight away.\n- **Backoff:** the wait doubles each time, `backoff * 2**attempt`. With the default `backoff=0.5`, it waits 0.5s after the first failure and 1s after the second.\n- **New setting:** `backoff` is an optional constructor argument, so existing callers don't need to change.\n- **Giving up:** if the third attempt also gets a 503, that error is passed back to the caller.\n- **Connections:** each failed 503 response is closed before the next try, so retries don't leave connections open.\n\nTest results:\n\n| Server responses | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200 | data returned | 1 |\n| 503, 200 | data returned | 2 |\n| 503, 503, 200 | data returned | 3 |\n| 503, 503, 503 | 503 error raised | 3 |\n| 500 | 500 error raised, no retry | 1 |\n| 503, 404 | 404 error raised | 2 |\n\nThe project has no test suite, so I didn't add one. These checks were a one-off script and aren't saved anywhere.\n\nConnection errors and timeouts (`URLError`) are not retried. You only asked for 503, but say if you want those retried too.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 69525, "requests_cache_write": 143848, "requests_cost_usd": 0.773821, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 2031, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial17", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 93, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:50:06.366172+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent